1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,224
I read my own obituary over lukewarm coffee, choking on words that declared me legally dead since dawn.

2
00:00:07,524 --> 00:00:14,748
The date printed at the top was today. My age, my address, even my childhood dog were all right there.

3
00:00:15,048 --> 00:00:22,608
Panic tightened my chest as I looked around the crowded diner, searching for the sick prankster responsible for this.

4
00:00:22,908 --> 00:00:33,060
Nobody was laughing. In fact, every single customer sat completely still, staring straight ahead in total, unbroken silence.

5
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:41,712
A shadow fell across the laminate table. The smell of old paper and winter rain drifted into my space.

6
00:00:42,012 --> 00:00:49,428
An elderly woman with kind, tired eyes pulled out the chair opposite me and sat down without asking.

7
00:00:49,728 --> 00:00:57,936
She tapped the obituary with a wrinkled finger. You always hated surprises, David, she whispered with a gentle smile.

8
00:00:58,236 --> 00:01:06,180
How do you know my name? I stammered, feeling the air grow suddenly heavy and cold around my lungs.

9
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:13,584
She turned the newspaper around. The ink on the page was still wet, shifting to spell out new sentences.

10
00:01:13,884 --> 00:01:19,212
If I died this morning in that car crash, who is breathing in my chest right now?
